linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe parallelogram $P$ is mapped to the parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ has vertices $(1,1),(0,0),(-1,1),$ and $(0,2).$ Which of the following are vertices of $P?$\n- **I.** $(0,-1)$\n- **II.** $(1,1)$\n- **III.** $(-1,0)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${P}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $P$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1-(-1)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $P$ are $(1,0),(0,0),(0,1),(1,1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357528 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0cbb889-0fe1-5347-94a3-53db3ff9a95c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Vertices of a Polygon Given Its Image Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2bc64c6-664a-5b24-aa66-f3eba12645eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469620} {:answer/id #uuid "c28bee52-3d67-53f6-ad56-642b64e05043" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c28bee52-3d67-53f6-ad56-642b64e05043" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469621} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3824387-31bc-52a2-846e-2cd22ab4bb71" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470422} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17d150ea-6336-53f3-9ff9-69a5bbd01ea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469622} {:answer/id #uuid "6ad7216c-e3b7-5ed2-868b-6a0ea8df964a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17d150ea-6336-53f3-9ff9-69a5bbd01ea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469622} :answer-field/id #uuid "60197c06-01e3-5c67-9cf2-3b20020bd750" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470423} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d91462d4-c453-51f4-a051-ec052973b66e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469624} {:answer/id #uuid "4b540585-d54d-5c51-a990-620c2d48bdfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d91462d4-c453-51f4-a051-ec052973b66e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469624} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf37dfab-4b60-5bca-be75-986b98bb898e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470424}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "56746454-856c-5001-bcf8-93772c0debce" :question/math-academy-id "q-9264" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe parallelogram $P$ is mapped to the parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ has vertices $(0,0),(-2,-2),(-4,0),$ and $(-2,2).$ Which of the following are vertices of $P?$\n- **I.** $(2,2)$\n- **II.** $(0,1)$\n- **III.** $(-2,0)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${P}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $P$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{-1-1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $P$ are $(0,0),(2,0),(2,2),(0,2).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357561 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a926134-0870-5528-985d-2c92e71158f4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Second-Order Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79f1d0cf-4c3f-5c5c-ae91-488ad20a8de2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469626} {:answer/id #uuid "e30119a6-2130-5938-bd90-71a9385d623b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e30119a6-2130-5938-bd90-71a9385d623b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469627} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c251103-3612-5cc7-947b-af5e3a307592" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470425} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ded283b-5f18-5f91-a519-dc6be52e9ffa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469628} {:answer/id #uuid "a2535307-1b92-5ff9-99d4-5185de5d303e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ded283b-5f18-5f91-a519-dc6be52e9ffa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469628} :answer-field/id #uuid "6733649c-0fec-5d08-b5ec-46452d2f3e60" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470426} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37c16826-1021-5383-bad1-77de256c244d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469630} {:answer/id #uuid "fd322604-9348-559d-8fe7-b3bba3d52b96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37c16826-1021-5383-bad1-77de256c244d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469630} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c67418e-c6a8-56c0-abda-6159ea8578fc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470427}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "95ad491b-4ee0-5e7b-8a0c-33d2b7cf1e9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-93715" :question/problem "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n- **I.** ${y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$\n- **II.** ${y}^{″}+y{y}^{′}=0$\n- **III.** $\\frac{1}{y}{y}^{″}+y=x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "А second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=1,b(x)=-x,c(x)=1,$ and $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+y{y}^{′}=0\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $y{y}^{′}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{y}{y}^{″}+y=x\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $\\frac{1}{y}{y}^{″}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357562 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a926134-0870-5528-985d-2c92e71158f4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Second-Order Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09a469b2-5896-588d-9b5f-f86452b44eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469632} {:answer/id #uuid "aca4c5d2-3985-5df0-8512-b4a193218a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09a469b2-5896-588d-9b5f-f86452b44eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469632} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2f92d40-06fd-5963-9b61-c9a8f2d37df8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470428} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7732c50a-196e-5bd4-ae46-9604b54c4cf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469634} {:answer/id #uuid "4c2401c4-e763-54a9-90ce-bd5138b0907a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c2401c4-e763-54a9-90ce-bd5138b0907a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469635} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c4a0149-404f-5dda-a8e0-57d0e7983147" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470429} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c20331be-786e-5ec8-92b5-cf500b578551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469636} {:answer/id #uuid "c09b531f-230e-59c8-a5d3-13154d41383b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c09b531f-230e-59c8-a5d3-13154d41383b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469637} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e6c792f-fb4d-56c6-a87c-d0da2370a750" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470430}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d6e8b60c-c6c9-5753-b254-94e3e9635292" :question/math-academy-id "q-93721" :question/problem "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n- **I.** $2{y}^{2}{y}^{″}-{e}^{x}{y}^{′}=x$\n- **II.** $\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$\n- **III.** ${y}^{″}+17y=2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "А second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n2{y}^{2}{y}^{″}-{e}^{x}{y}^{′}=x\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $2{y}^{2}{y}^{″}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=\\frac{1}{x},b(x)=1,c(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ and $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+17y=2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=1,b(x)=0,c(x)=17,$ and $f(x)=2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357611 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161979 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c2da07e-23b5-58d0-aeef-14e21b329368" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Symmetric Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b67bf2d-f434-5cbf-a65f-fe92576ed3fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469638} {:answer/id #uuid "1f304f6a-e85b-5ca9-8056-745663c7ef23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b67bf2d-f434-5cbf-a65f-fe92576ed3fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469638} :answer-field/id #uuid "04035bc7-0baa-52a2-8819-5785c4397711" :answer-field/key "P" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470431} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a25bb71a-4230-5f5d-aaf6-2df76c7f39c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469640} {:answer/id #uuid "82cc5f65-1d57-56f6-b5fe-cc38b670cf45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82cc5f65-1d57-56f6-b5fe-cc38b670cf45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469641} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9c0a8bf-9374-501d-9297-e531eb25d3f0" :answer-field/key "Q" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470432} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "689daa18-2b9c-5f89-9c4a-2575e6717d8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469642} {:answer/id #uuid "2223f70f-5ec1-579a-a3a0-521b192241b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "689daa18-2b9c-5f89-9c4a-2575e6717d8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469642} :answer-field/id #uuid "800cf770-f16d-5241-92e2-0bfe2665859c" :answer-field/key "R" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470433}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "225f8bdf-5da4-5137-973e-d6466e5f7f7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-93985" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are symmetric?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $P$ is *not* a symmetric matrix. Since ${p}_{12}\\ne {p}_{21},$ we obtain $P\\ne {P}^{T}.$\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $Q$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $Q={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $R$ is *not* a symmetric matrix. Since ${r}_{12}\\ne {r}_{21},$ we obtain $R\\ne {R}^{T}.$\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Q$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357612 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161979 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c2da07e-23b5-58d0-aeef-14e21b329368" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Symmetric Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ff75887-303a-5746-8422-c3fbabd4f7a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469650} {:answer/id #uuid "4211df5c-427d-5871-91ca-25355a0f4f5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4211df5c-427d-5871-91ca-25355a0f4f5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469651} :answer-field/id #uuid "6120ed4f-d1c8-52d5-b05f-940b21c87fed" :answer-field/key "P" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470437} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bac5279c-5373-583f-86b8-d00181c474b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469652} {:answer/id #uuid "6947fc2e-4eb6-525c-bc29-51468a7e4538" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bac5279c-5373-583f-86b8-d00181c474b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469652} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e18af8a-2b61-5dcf-af19-0e391a4da342" :answer-field/key "Q" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470438} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6db29846-2fc2-5ef9-8d0e-157f02a4a2a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469654} {:answer/id #uuid "3808bdfa-f327-5c13-b5d5-663088e525e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3808bdfa-f327-5c13-b5d5-663088e525e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469655} :answer-field/id #uuid "b72c82db-3efb-5c9a-9d57-f990f418cde7" :answer-field/key "R" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470439}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cc49e39d-dc41-5d92-84ab-b1310e571077" :question/math-academy-id "q-93988" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are symmetric?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{2} & 7 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $P$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $P={P}^{T}.$\n\n- $Q$ is *not* a symmetric matrix. Since ${q}_{12}\\ne {q}_{21},$ we obtain $Q\\ne {Q}^{T}.$\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $R$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $R={R}^{T}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $R$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357613 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161979 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c2da07e-23b5-58d0-aeef-14e21b329368" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Symmetric Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e79675c-d340-558d-85a1-f9f7b1029de9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469662} {:answer/id #uuid "60bd1f0c-8a39-5c12-8e0f-a94ebe34fcb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e79675c-d340-558d-85a1-f9f7b1029de9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469662} :answer-field/id #uuid "579a2afb-cfc8-5b6a-b249-9a478ce20513" :answer-field/key "P" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470443} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b879cd8-8163-5323-9891-635c9985bcba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469664} {:answer/id #uuid "607d0264-5580-5201-bc08-95e2af57eb0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "607d0264-5580-5201-bc08-95e2af57eb0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469665} :answer-field/id #uuid "a537cbd9-73a4-5a02-9dd4-d84d4bc3cef5" :answer-field/key "Q" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470444} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff91e8eb-90ca-5476-9dd7-9c0f537bc20b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469666} {:answer/id #uuid "9efe100a-3cc8-5748-85a8-5c7f40e3cdb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff91e8eb-90ca-5476-9dd7-9c0f537bc20b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469666} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e526195-935e-5f64-8850-034ecc34b49e" :answer-field/key "R" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470445}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0a5f4b21-f8de-5f12-8b8c-c4be1021742e" :question/math-academy-id "q-93993" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are symmetric?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\sqrt{5} & -1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $P$ is *not* a symmetric matrix. Since ${p}_{13}\\ne {p}_{31},$ we obtain $P\\ne {P}^{T}.$\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $Q$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $Q={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $R$ is *not* a symmetric matrix. Since ${r}_{12}\\ne {r}_{21},$ we obtain $R\\ne {R}^{T}.$\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Q$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357639 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161984 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e62e458d-0724-5dbe-b448-b79404f279f9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices of Quadratic Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65093f23-78c7-51de-a363-9dbf483a2119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469668} {:answer/id #uuid "e3df6bc6-63f0-58f1-b185-9f86ffe8f132" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3df6bc6-63f0-58f1-b185-9f86ffe8f132" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469669} :answer-field/id #uuid "975b133f-d74b-51d2-abee-2ea32191fb78" :answer-field/key "K" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470446} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64b2294d-cee4-57bb-b2b3-e9f02a2402ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469670} {:answer/id #uuid "20eae9d6-2c44-536a-8eb2-c357b015ca69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20eae9d6-2c44-536a-8eb2-c357b015ca69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469671} :answer-field/id #uuid "754fc5e3-20bb-552f-9086-00972a64ad00" :answer-field/key "L" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470447} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69f33c3f-be58-5c23-81dd-d2484c6e27b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469672} {:answer/id #uuid "4adc5058-528d-5d28-acec-3db27a965ea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69f33c3f-be58-5c23-81dd-d2484c6e27b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469672} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b9d8951-1ed6-52a8-9476-b293978d9255" :answer-field/key "M" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470448}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "df2ac6ff-519f-58d2-90f1-c2ccb3e51740" :question/math-academy-id "q-94059" :question/problem "Which of the following could be matrices of quadratic forms defined on ${R}^{2}?$\n\n$$\nK=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,L=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,M=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that every quadratic form defined on ${R}^{2}$ has an associated $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $K$ could be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{2}$ since it is a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix.\n\n- $L$ could also be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{2}$ since it is a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix.\n\n- $M$ *cannot* be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{2}.$ Although it's a $2\\times 2$ matrix, $M$ is not symmetric since ${m}_{12}\\ne {m}_{21}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$K$ and $L$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357640 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161984 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e62e458d-0724-5dbe-b448-b79404f279f9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices of Quadratic Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d31c7c30-6a09-537a-838e-26380db70980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469674} {:answer/id #uuid "92cf1571-c53f-56df-9ea1-722039f4a649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92cf1571-c53f-56df-9ea1-722039f4a649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469675} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5e87bb9-4337-5d11-b331-cb149719d64c" :answer-field/key "T" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470449} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c2b6548-8685-5790-bfe5-2d560d2cc7c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469676} {:answer/id #uuid "db963199-3d93-524d-9ddc-762de74a136c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db963199-3d93-524d-9ddc-762de74a136c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469677} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccc8546e-485b-59af-b253-732df91bd451" :answer-field/key "U" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470450} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5a63cd7-c1d9-5588-9330-fe1036e53e50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469678} {:answer/id #uuid "c7b3920e-c0f7-5a98-ac0a-e6120f9c52d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5a63cd7-c1d9-5588-9330-fe1036e53e50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469678} :answer-field/id #uuid "431b9dde-c58c-5f17-a803-fb9e8caef06e" :answer-field/key "V" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470451}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "93d6f7f1-c1fb-5ae2-b8f7-98ecf5b306a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-94062" :question/problem "Which of the following could be matrices of quadratic forms defined on ${R}^{3}?$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -8 \\\\ -3 & -8 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that every quadratic form defined on ${R}^{3}$ has an associated $3\\times 3$ symmetric matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $T$ could be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{3}$ since it is a $3\\times 3$ symmetric matrix.\n\n- $U$ could also be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{3}$ since it is a $3\\times 3$ symmetric matrix.\n\n- $V$ *cannot* be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{3}$ since it's a $2\\times 2$ matrix (not $3\\times 3$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$T$ and $U$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357641 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161984 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e62e458d-0724-5dbe-b448-b79404f279f9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices of Quadratic Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "276e7784-3f27-5f16-857d-565398b07228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469680} {:answer/id #uuid "8c5031f6-651d-54a5-875f-0765312ac751" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "276e7784-3f27-5f16-857d-565398b07228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469680} :answer-field/id #uuid "aaf3a840-0c3e-54a1-a75f-fef852021152" :answer-field/key "D" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470452} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c5ba6a4-f5a4-5d3c-9783-20a15cdf47fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469682} {:answer/id #uuid "bd4c060c-f0ed-573f-9f2e-325a2e5ab7da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c5ba6a4-f5a4-5d3c-9783-20a15cdf47fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469682} :answer-field/id #uuid "f59b0a79-de63-5dfc-b585-7bed00e3a9b0" :answer-field/key "E" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470453} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b9e0823-8dcb-5fde-8a80-d56b3d3c5c13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469684} {:answer/id #uuid "7d60c142-4a85-5115-8734-c4470d6fadb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d60c142-4a85-5115-8734-c4470d6fadb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469685} :answer-field/id #uuid "e58d9eb0-2376-5e45-b12e-a50de55ab094" :answer-field/key "F" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470454}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "61630213-687e-509d-b369-4384ce08371c" :question/math-academy-id "q-94063" :question/problem "Which of the following could be matrices of quadratic forms defined on ${R}^{4}?$\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,F=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that every quadratic form defined on ${R}^{4}$ has an associated $4\\times 4$ symmetric matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $D$ *cannot* be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{4}.$ Although it's a $4\\times 4$ matrix, $D$ is not symmetric since ${d}_{24}\\ne {d}_{42}.$\n\n- $E$ *cannot* be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{4}$ since it's a $2\\times 2$ matrix (not $4\\times 4$).\n\n- $F$ could be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{4}$ since it is a $4\\times 4$ symmetric matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$F$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357712 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147430 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e17fe7fc-3b85-5f2c-aa69-2336b05b16b2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to Simple Harmonic Motion Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91cc05c9-21e6-5e57-ab36-d1e4df3c1b68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469686} {:answer/id #uuid "768d503e-91ff-5b08-aeae-dda02d324c1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91cc05c9-21e6-5e57-ab36-d1e4df3c1b68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469686} :answer-field/id #uuid "683d9c93-8fa5-5d1a-98f2-20d68cd20554" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470455} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54fdca8a-daf1-5068-9ae9-279b847a3c10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469688} {:answer/id #uuid "6e0e45cd-9729-5b3a-98b9-20bb12012d86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54fdca8a-daf1-5068-9ae9-279b847a3c10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469688} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac2ab10a-f022-5c38-8a87-3bfd67d0c187" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470456} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6699d8e-9150-5a70-b4dc-ca5c4bf1ec18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469690} {:answer/id #uuid "21d5c538-57b2-5322-8c9a-786a358047e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21d5c538-57b2-5322-8c9a-786a358047e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469691} :answer-field/id #uuid "3688a682-49fd-5cdc-b69d-7a273c82d6dc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470457}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b779ea2-64c9-5921-9b3e-0c6d8313380f" :question/math-academy-id "q-94275" :question/problem "A particle is moving with simple harmonic motion. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4y=0.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n\nI. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n\nII. $y=R\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n\nIII. $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t$\n\nNote that $R,{ϕ}_{1},{ϕ}_{2},A$ and $B$ are constants.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The SHM equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nThe general solution to the SHM equation can be written in three different forms:\n\n1\\. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n\n2\\. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n\n3\\. $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=4\\,⟹\\,\\omega =2.\n$$\n\nThus, we have:\n\n1\\. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n\n2\\. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n\n3\\. $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t$\n\nTherefore, only function III could be used to represent $y(t).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357713 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147430 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e17fe7fc-3b85-5f2c-aa69-2336b05b16b2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to Simple Harmonic Motion Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ad2732d-69c4-58f7-a030-9480b5996e1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469692} {:answer/id #uuid "69b705cb-b59f-52e9-becb-0449feb134d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69b705cb-b59f-52e9-becb-0449feb134d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469693} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ecc5cf1-fd33-54bd-a9b6-52159bbfb77b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470458} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e486e67-136c-5f23-a046-eac73e44bc12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469694} {:answer/id #uuid "c3d68160-8c63-5214-9a73-525ffab0890b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3d68160-8c63-5214-9a73-525ffab0890b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469695} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ddcdebe-f528-5f7e-8339-afd49564c830" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470459} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8340b1ea-d19d-5867-beea-5ece4a646047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469696} {:answer/id #uuid "6418afea-2aff-5470-8cd8-97afc5b4b6ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8340b1ea-d19d-5867-beea-5ece4a646047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469696} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c9a9501-aa24-5bf0-b66c-51ecefe82cb3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "784be4fd-7d61-5b65-af33-15597c14ae36" :question/math-academy-id "q-94276" :question/problem "A particle is moving with simple harmonic motion. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+16y=0.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n- **I.** $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n- **II.** $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n- **III.** $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡16t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡16t$\n\nNote that $R,{ϕ}_{1},{ϕ}_{2},A$ and $B$ are constants.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The SHM equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nThe general solution to the SHM equation can be written in three different forms:\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=16\\,⟹\\,\\omega =4.\n$$\n\nThus, we have:\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t$\n\nTherefore, only functions I and II could be used to represent $y(t).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357736 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147450 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "813ec1d4-93ec-5a9e-996f-b2e672714927" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to Forced Harmonic Motion Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97ea5463-bea1-5eaf-bc15-3836a5ba47fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469698} {:answer/id #uuid "07fd1def-dfaa-5ec4-ae66-bd968103e02f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07fd1def-dfaa-5ec4-ae66-bd968103e02f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469699} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c1229eb-a220-5d64-9dde-8d4198484535" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470461} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e48f9942-dc1d-5bfd-8c7e-fffcfc58f5c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469700} {:answer/id #uuid "cd7c7638-d189-5ef7-8aee-3f80c8472788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e48f9942-dc1d-5bfd-8c7e-fffcfc58f5c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469700} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8f4b973-4fd4-5ee7-97b7-671e55562e4d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470462} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35c12017-b6ff-5bed-a4ab-944b10eb21be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469702} {:answer/id #uuid "62d36b84-29c6-5fca-991c-d87a064eec38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35c12017-b6ff-5bed-a4ab-944b10eb21be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469702} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ef40f75-93cb-5ffc-a30d-cf9bc3956155" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470463}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "feaf4026-120d-5dc5-a147-ce0975029f64" :question/math-academy-id "q-94376" :question/problem "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n- **I.** $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+ϕ)-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n- **II.** $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+ϕ)+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$\n- **III.** $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R$ and $ϕ$ are constants.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The general solution to this equation is the sum of the complementary function and a particular solution.\n\nFirst, we find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(t),$ which is the solution to the simple harmonic motion equation ${y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.$\nIt can be written in three different forms:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=1\\,⟹\\,\\omega =1.\n$$\n\nThus, we have:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$\n\nNext, we find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(t).$ The particular solution is of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=t(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡t).\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution into the differential equation and equating coefficients, we find that $\\alpha =-1$ and $\\beta =0.$ So, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+ϕ)-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+ϕ)-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n\nOnly I matches the forms above. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357737 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147450 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "813ec1d4-93ec-5a9e-996f-b2e672714927" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to Forced Harmonic Motion Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edd47e7d-f7e3-5d97-920b-4415df8afc73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469704} {:answer/id #uuid "b1947615-a621-5c38-a8b2-65f39eb8f335" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edd47e7d-f7e3-5d97-920b-4415df8afc73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469704} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ace747d-85b7-53e5-9b79-77234909c714" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470464} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7714d7d-abaa-5ea7-a556-ace61b6af7f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469706} {:answer/id #uuid "ba17faad-e264-5d00-9e6e-97a82564376d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba17faad-e264-5d00-9e6e-97a82564376d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469707} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f5d49b4-18b3-5548-b0aa-1dd4be52ea6e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470465} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28bd472a-6d85-58a8-8448-7f1562ef06d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469708} {:answer/id #uuid "8d5eaa3c-7699-5df1-8c11-cb3fcbeed6f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28bd472a-6d85-58a8-8448-7f1562ef06d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469708} :answer-field/id #uuid "60fcc67d-062a-5c14-a57e-7491a704df6b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470466}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "91ea3a27-d7dd-5526-bebd-b64e4b8069b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-94377" :question/problem "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+16y=32t.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n\nI. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+ϕ)+16t$\n\nII. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t+ϕ)+2t$\n\nIII. $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+8t$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R$ and $ϕ$ are constants.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The general solution is the sum of the complementary solution and the particular solution:\n\n$$\ny(t)={y}_{c}(t)+{y}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(t),$ which is the solution to the simple harmonic motion equation ${y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.$ It can be written in three different forms:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=16\\,⟹\\,\\omega =4.\n$$\n\nThus, we have:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t$\n\nNext, we find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(t).$ Since the external force is a linear function, we assume that the particular solution is also a linear function,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\alpha t+\\beta .\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution into the differential equation and equating coefficients, we find that $\\alpha =2$ and $\\beta =0.$ So, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=2t.\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t+ϕ)+2t, \\\\ y(t) & =R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t+ϕ)+2t, \\\\ y(t) & =A\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t+2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOnly II matches the forms above. Therefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357739 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147450 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "813ec1d4-93ec-5a9e-996f-b2e672714927" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to Forced Harmonic Motion Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d1ebf5f6-1eef-504e-a45a-429288ea176d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469710} {:answer/id #uuid "d729886d-e293-59ee-8ca1-95ce2767b7cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1ebf5f6-1eef-504e-a45a-429288ea176d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469710} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc17f441-34f0-56a4-9634-da126b593dac" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470467} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d37c668-cc5e-5675-93e6-5b054ee0aa13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469712} {:answer/id #uuid "b62dc90a-7763-5dd6-ab0f-bba731e10dfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d37c668-cc5e-5675-93e6-5b054ee0aa13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469712} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1424c1d-310b-5a93-8997-a3196feaf7c2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470468} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7dcc6e6-2f3f-50ce-bc07-ef3040ceb432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469714} {:answer/id #uuid "b57fed2a-9162-538c-8c97-cb589188adbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b57fed2a-9162-538c-8c97-cb589188adbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469715} :answer-field/id #uuid "a58e0ec3-0615-5a4e-a8b8-13cb290e43b9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470469}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cbe86c7f-4360-5aea-8ad0-c457c70df4e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-94382" :question/problem "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+25y=24\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n\nI. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(25t+ϕ)+12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$\n\nII. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t+ϕ)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n\nIII. $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R$ and $ϕ$ are constants.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The general solution to this equation is the sum of the complementary function and a particular solution.\n\nFirst, we find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(t),$ which is the solution to the simple harmonic motion equation ${y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.$ It can be written in three different forms:\n\n1\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)$\n\n2\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)$\n\n3\\. ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=25\\,⟹\\,\\omega =5.\n$$\n\nThus, we have:\n\n1\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t+ϕ)$\n\n2\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t+ϕ)$\n\n3\\. ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t$\n\nNext, we find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(t).$ The particular solution is of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution into the differential equation and equating coefficients, we find that $\\alpha =1$ and $\\beta =0.$ So, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n1\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t+ϕ)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n\n2\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t+ϕ)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n\n3\\. ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n\nOnly III matches the forms above. Therefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357740 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147450 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "813ec1d4-93ec-5a9e-996f-b2e672714927" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to Forced Harmonic Motion Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cae621f-3d6e-5d45-9b65-1fad41f795f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469716} {:answer/id #uuid "21ad5055-2b76-5888-b77e-0849f5f11837" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21ad5055-2b76-5888-b77e-0849f5f11837" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469717} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed908e42-450b-5534-9da1-729e23bf4ae6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470470} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc52e9e4-97b0-5304-be16-59ad68d87273" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469718} {:answer/id #uuid "8278a36c-ae51-5440-b66c-2b9da7b262a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc52e9e4-97b0-5304-be16-59ad68d87273" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469718} :answer-field/id #uuid "1847518c-ebde-5827-8e28-1cc95c28b40a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470471} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a44e8621-e0a4-5954-b461-751df8afdcb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469720} {:answer/id #uuid "60960cba-b7ee-5e40-a9ae-22c295ee5156" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a44e8621-e0a4-5954-b461-751df8afdcb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469720} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3f659e9-9050-529d-929a-3c5358c2751f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0cf314c8-ddb9-53cd-832f-d87f0d4562fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-94383" :question/problem "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion with damping. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+41y=10{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n- **I.** $y={e}^{-4t}(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t)+\\frac{{e}^{t}}{5}$\n- **II.** $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9t+ϕ)+\\frac{{e}^{t}}{5}$\n- **III.** $y=R{e}^{-4t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t+ϕ)+10{e}^{t}$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R$ and $ϕ$ are constants.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The general solution is the sum of the complementary solution and the particular solution:\n\n$$\ny(t)={y}_{c}(t)+{y}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(t),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation ${y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+41y=0.$ Writing down and solving the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +41 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +16)-16+41 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +4)^{2}+25 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +4)^{2} & =-25 \\\\ \\lambda +4 & =\\pm 5\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-4\\pm 5\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(t)$ can be expressed in any of the following forms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{c}(t) & ={e}^{-4t}(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t), \\\\ {y}_{c}(t) & =R{e}^{-4t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t+ϕ), \\\\ {y}_{c}(t) & =R{e}^{-4t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t+ϕ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(t).$ The particular solution is of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\alpha {e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution into the differential equation and equating coefficients, we find that $\\alpha =\\frac{1}{5}.$ So, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\frac{{e}^{t}}{5}.\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & ={e}^{-4t}(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t)+\\frac{{e}^{t}}{5}, \\\\ y(t) & =R{e}^{-4t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t+ϕ)+\\frac{{e}^{t}}{5}, \\\\ y(t) & =R{e}^{-4t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t+ϕ)+\\frac{{e}^{t}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOnly I matches the forms above. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360479 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6289ad34-2393-5f5f-b7f0-a1ab1a3916f4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Possible Quadratic Form Types Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "491282d8-087a-5b6a-872d-6b0a47d66b84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469722} {:answer/id #uuid "06e9071d-b647-5c18-bb45-e68fcc570e3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "491282d8-087a-5b6a-872d-6b0a47d66b84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469722} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef7d7514-e7a3-5427-b315-a9a69bce3495" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470473} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83d2a2f4-ca6f-5c88-a824-d7acfdea58ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469724} {:answer/id #uuid "95ece7a6-9e69-5e78-8957-46a3c4175115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95ece7a6-9e69-5e78-8957-46a3c4175115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469725} :answer-field/id #uuid "64c56b6b-2880-560b-9538-f33060b8721c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470474} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5da7956-0eb9-5adb-bdb6-5c327d8b35b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469726} {:answer/id #uuid "91c1f39d-20a8-532f-b2ef-a41f48e42975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91c1f39d-20a8-532f-b2ef-a41f48e42975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469727} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4dd36d1-3aac-54c6-b8e2-1006ae8abc43" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470475}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "96ce050e-6292-5b2a-b7c7-0c1f7f51192d" :question/math-academy-id "q-94731" :question/problem "$$\n\n$$\n\nConsider the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ By evaluating the following quadratic forms at $x$ **only,** determine which of them **cannot** be negative-definite.\n- **I.** $R(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}$\n- **II.** $S(x)={x}^{T}\\,[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]x$\n- **III.** $T(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A quadratic form $Q(x)$ is negative-definite if $Q(x)<0$ for all $x\\in {R}^{n}∖{0}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the quadratic forms by substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]:$\n\n- Quadratic form I *might* be negative-definite. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(x) & =(-1)^{2}-{3}^{2} \\\\  & =1-9 \\\\  & =-8<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Quadratic form II *cannot* be negative-definite since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =33>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Quadratic form III *cannot* be negative-definite since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(x) & =(-1)^{2}+3(3)^{2} \\\\  & =1+27 \\\\  & =28>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360480 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6289ad34-2393-5f5f-b7f0-a1ab1a3916f4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Possible Quadratic Form Types Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "195d16b7-57d2-5a98-ad60-1a8888bb7b27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469728} {:answer/id #uuid "4588d0a9-3d54-5976-bc71-51d75a7695f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "195d16b7-57d2-5a98-ad60-1a8888bb7b27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469728} :answer-field/id #uuid "37ef1083-cbd3-5fa2-b49e-f0aa3bd44d3f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470476} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dba4d436-16f6-5071-b037-fe3017f476b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469730} {:answer/id #uuid "5afbfc12-a6d2-5021-8f8e-5141947c51a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5afbfc12-a6d2-5021-8f8e-5141947c51a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469731} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ad01140-9faf-5249-96a3-7f505c7b7804" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470477} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7f022e9-09a5-5650-8334-9f2aff11f4c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469732} {:answer/id #uuid "b36fdf26-1340-5fc8-be86-56dcbc4ad2c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469733}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b36fdf26-1340-5fc8-be86-56dcbc4ad2c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469733} :answer-field/id #uuid "4676be30-c32d-51b3-b92b-dc162406a163" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470478}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8c28bdf3-28d7-5fd9-bd3d-116dde5b3b96" :question/math-academy-id "q-94734" :question/problem "$$\n\n$$\n\nConsider the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].$ By evaluating the following quadratic forms at $x$ **only,** determine which of them **cannot** be positive-definite.\n- **I.** $R(x)={x}_{2}^{2}+7{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$\n- **II.** $S(x)={x}^{T}\\,[\\begin{aligned}7 & -9 \\\\ -9 & -2\\end{aligned}]x$\n- **III.** $T(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}-3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A quadratic form $Q(x)$ is positive-definite if $Q(x)>0$ for all $x\\in {R}^{n}∖{0}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the quadratic forms by substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]:$\n\n- Quadratic form I *might* be positive-definite. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(x) & =(-6)^{2}+7\\cdot 0\\cdot (-6) \\\\  & =36+0 \\\\  & =36>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Quadratic form II *cannot* be positive-definite since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 & -9 \\\\ -9 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}54 & 12\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-72<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Quadratic form III *cannot* be positive-definite since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(x) & ={0}^{2}-(-6)^{2}-3\\cdot 0\\cdot (-6) \\\\  & =-36-0 \\\\  & =-36<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360498 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162009 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4105f1cb-eb48-5946-92f7-cd5e67689912" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Form Type by Calculating the Corresponding Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abae4a38-c5fd-5f02-a772-5aa129094bed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469734} {:answer/id #uuid "61d28482-9aa5-5496-9fe2-e88afd3b2c83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abae4a38-c5fd-5f02-a772-5aa129094bed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469734} :answer-field/id #uuid "1888ce5d-ffbd-5ed4-8be1-6bd4f78e3048" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470479} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c36a82ef-f663-5517-a82d-dfb31295d4df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469736} {:answer/id #uuid "1abaa9d3-1384-5eab-9d1f-4167841b8420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469737}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c36a82ef-f663-5517-a82d-dfb31295d4df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469736} :answer-field/id #uuid "78bab090-2cec-52a7-8c1a-ea25848b4605" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470480} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8053ba89-f2f1-5607-8419-7cfe23f95b4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469738} {:answer/id #uuid "2a6d6721-833a-5366-b67a-9b57255478fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a6d6721-833a-5366-b67a-9b57255478fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469739} :answer-field/id #uuid "24fa5bdc-7dac-5793-b27a-1eadf77bbfa1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470481}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1a997acb-de91-5ebd-a6cc-103226757603" :question/math-academy-id "q-94787" :question/problem "Which of the following quadratic forms over ${R}^{2}$ are positive-definite?\n- **I.** ${x}^{T}\\,Qx,$ where the eigenvalues of $Q$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=0$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=3$\n- **II.** ${x}^{T}\\,Rx,$ where the eigenvalues of $R$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-6$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=10$\n- **III.** ${x}^{T}\\,Sx,$ where the eigenvalues of $S$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=5$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=8$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given a quadratic form $Q(x)={x}^{T}Ax,$ we have the following theorem:\n\n- $Q$ is positive-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are positive,\n\n- $Q$ is positive semi-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are non-negative (note that positive semi-definite quadratic forms include all positive-definite quadratic forms),\n\n- $Q$ is negative-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are negative,\n\n- $Q$ is negative semi-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are non-positive (note that negative semi-definite quadratic forms include all negative-definite quadratic forms), and\n\n- $Q$ is indefinite if and only if $A$ has both positive and negative eigenvalues.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our quadratic forms in turn.\n\n- Quadratic form I is *not* positive-definite since not all of the eigenvalues of $Q$ are positive (for example, ${\\lambda }_{1}=0$ is not positive).\n\n- Quadratic form II is *not* positive-definite since not all of the eigenvalues of $R$ are positive (${\\lambda }_{1}=-6$ is not positive).\n\n- Quadratic form III is positive-definite. Indeed, all of the eigenvalues of $S$ are positive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360587 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152220 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aee17e3a-031d-5c0e-9488-17410b3a2372" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Dimensions of Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d187c9b-4747-5283-9bc9-8efe09e8060f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469740} {:answer/id #uuid "20710a64-a1f6-53b9-bb87-89bbb120ac13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20710a64-a1f6-53b9-bb87-89bbb120ac13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469741} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a78ce37-f314-5d92-89e5-1a4e69816762" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470482} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fb53497-1373-537c-ab6b-c275065368ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469742} {:answer/id #uuid "54e914c8-6da4-5745-92df-18376215c8bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fb53497-1373-537c-ab6b-c275065368ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469742} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e4f5ef9-09dd-5817-be5c-a500d256994f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470483} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32dacfc1-43b3-5acf-9309-2e3b2734039d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469744} {:answer/id #uuid "e3025dbb-dc9d-5875-bbde-386a8b48d96a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469745}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3025dbb-dc9d-5875-bbde-386a8b48d96a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469745} :answer-field/id #uuid "08b368a7-6b1c-5b89-bb11-36ed15b2a1e2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470484}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bc2e74a2-6b3b-5817-8831-ae21a9740417" :question/math-academy-id "q-95226" :question/problem "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $15?$\n- **I.** ${\\text{M}}_{3\\times 5}(R),$ the vector space of all $3\\times 5$ matrices over $R$\n- **II.** ${R}_{15}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $15$\n- **III.** ${R}^{15}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{3\\times 5}(R))=3\\cdot 5=15.\\,✓\n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{15}[t])=15+1=16\\ne 15.\\,\\times \n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{15})=15.\\,✓\n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360588 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152220 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aee17e3a-031d-5c0e-9488-17410b3a2372" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Dimensions of Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fcec67c5-760e-5bea-867c-1f8538390a0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469746} {:answer/id #uuid "a45b102a-a9cd-5e62-bef4-ff976a8a4364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469747}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcec67c5-760e-5bea-867c-1f8538390a0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469746} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c99cc93-ab7e-526d-8c1b-afd6b7c1efb8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470485} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e55b339b-2677-5880-8bca-04abfed3b198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469748} {:answer/id #uuid "8f4523f1-a870-579b-9c72-8b42af71fac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f4523f1-a870-579b-9c72-8b42af71fac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469749} :answer-field/id #uuid "12c20e3a-1a8e-5230-9418-c5642309849f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470486} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b70cad7-d2e6-5407-92c3-9876bd8334bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469750} {:answer/id #uuid "33567368-c4d0-5c09-893a-72d1923dd47c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469751}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33567368-c4d0-5c09-893a-72d1923dd47c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469751} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f7ef2c7-3be1-5bd5-821c-ff3415133f31" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470487}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "16544b73-f58b-552e-b996-d814ec3fa819" :question/math-academy-id "q-95230" :question/problem "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $36?$\n- **I.** ${R}_{6}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $6$\n- **II.** ${\\text{M}}_{12\\times 3}(R),$ the vector space of all $12\\times 3$ matrices over $R$\n- **III.** ${R}^{36}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{6}[t])=6+1=7\\ne 36.\\,\\times \n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{12\\times 3}(R))=12\\cdot 3=36.\\,✓\n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{36})=36.\\,✓\n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360589 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152221 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e609aabf-7e7e-5997-b8dc-c66e7a14a36f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Finite and Infinite-Dimensional Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfb76c40-7724-5451-8aac-19d2a8b57bd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469752} {:answer/id #uuid "c8f44b9f-b85e-5529-ac9f-fe0670b28b81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469753}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8f44b9f-b85e-5529-ac9f-fe0670b28b81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469753} :answer-field/id #uuid "73b049e3-3f6a-5ae0-9695-c15b320edad7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470488} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bbe85bc-6a5b-5101-83b8-3cbc7f9dadf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469754} {:answer/id #uuid "6ab4000e-252f-55bb-ae53-9aff79c28b25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bbe85bc-6a5b-5101-83b8-3cbc7f9dadf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469754} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4771de7-dcbb-5f3d-b4f0-14014f000a86" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470489} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "725da332-7f7a-56cd-b1c7-eb7e1e678523" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469756} {:answer/id #uuid "72759b00-fedb-5a37-ab83-88c976d1613c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72759b00-fedb-5a37-ab83-88c976d1613c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469757} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd7d2395-b54b-5c6b-a214-dab27c08b450" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470490}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9ccb2591-5640-5714-9681-7f41d3b4bf27" :question/math-academy-id "q-95239" :question/problem "Which of the following vector spaces are finite-dimensional?\n- **I.** ${R}^{200}$\n- **II.** $R[t],$ the vector space of all polynomial functions in the variable $t$\n- **III.** ${\\text{M}}_{200}(R),$ the vector space of all $200\\times 200$ matrices over $R$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our vector spaces.\n\n- $R[t]$ is *not* finite-dimensional. To understand why, we first note that the following set of (polynomial) functions is linearly independent:\n\n$$\n{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,…,{t}^{n}},\\,n\\in N.\n$$\n\nIndeed, we have that \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n}{a}_{i}{t}^{i}=0\n$$\n\nfor all $t\\in R$ if and only if ${a}_{i}=0$ for all $i=0,1,2,…,n.$ Therefore,  for any  $n\\in N,$  there exists a linearly independent subset of $R[t]$ of size $n,$ which imples that $R[t]$ cannot have finite dimension.\n\n- ${\\text{M}}_{200}(R)$ and ${R}^{200}$ are finite-dimensional. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{200}(R))={200}^{2}=40\\,000,\n$$\n\n \nand\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{200})=200\n$$\n\nare both finite numbers.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360590 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152221 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e609aabf-7e7e-5997-b8dc-c66e7a14a36f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Finite and Infinite-Dimensional Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "021e2b2f-1cfa-5e7f-a34a-b7f2570312cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469758} {:answer/id #uuid "bdb72ca2-146b-5bb8-8385-38863e97843d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdb72ca2-146b-5bb8-8385-38863e97843d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469759} :answer-field/id #uuid "29eb04aa-7838-546a-bb99-32c656373b29" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470491} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4771ff23-e6f3-5c09-9038-6c2677900baa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469760} {:answer/id #uuid "e7201a40-a402-5dd1-be24-316d02c7b70f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7201a40-a402-5dd1-be24-316d02c7b70f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469761} :answer-field/id #uuid "67e735b4-4170-55a6-b050-658c79ff7a90" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470492} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d82bb2f-ac86-5000-956c-61719812870d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469762} {:answer/id #uuid "e939c23c-8529-587d-843f-30d45e082086" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e939c23c-8529-587d-843f-30d45e082086" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469763} :answer-field/id #uuid "0531dddc-ea4a-5f2c-bd79-4fdd1a0039fc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470493}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7e94aa3d-a675-513e-b4ce-d62e1028540d" :question/math-academy-id "q-95240" :question/problem "Which of the following vector spaces are finite-dimensional?\n- **I.** ${R}_{1000}[t],$ the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $1\\,000$\n- **II.** ${\\text{M}}_{200\\times 500}(R),$ the vector space of all $200\\times 500$ matrices over $R$\n- **III.** $C,$ as a vector space over $R$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our vector spaces.\n\n- ${R}_{1000}[t]$ and ${\\text{M}}_{200\\times 500}(R)$ are finite-dimensional. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{1000}[t])=1\\,000+1=1\\,001,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{200\\times 500}(R))=200\\cdot 500=100\\,000\n$$\n\n \nare both finite numbers.\n\n- $C$ is also finite-dimensional. To understand why, we first note that the following set of complex numbers is linearly independent:\n\n$$\n{1,i}\n$$\n\nIndeed, we have that \n\n$$\na\\cdot 1+b\\cdot i=0\n$$\n\nif and only if $a=0$ and $b=0.$ Since our vector space is also spanned by this linearly independent subset, we have that $\\text{dim}(C)=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360591 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152221 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e609aabf-7e7e-5997-b8dc-c66e7a14a36f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Finite and Infinite-Dimensional Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fff98bb-e972-5f11-846c-673da276908b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469764} {:answer/id #uuid "d45189a1-3641-5b6e-bc82-14e18351dd20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d45189a1-3641-5b6e-bc82-14e18351dd20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469765} :answer-field/id #uuid "cba1ab4e-e5bb-53f1-9c1f-f43600de1e56" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470494} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38c04695-3316-50c3-9351-d72aef2be388" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469766} {:answer/id #uuid "962f0cfc-b7b6-507d-b809-7c7c5b4c8149" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38c04695-3316-50c3-9351-d72aef2be388" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469766} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa9d1ebc-2b43-53f9-b831-7c289b7e7867" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470495} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6117e42-4bf6-5334-b2cf-d997fb374102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469768} {:answer/id #uuid "af081fd9-07d5-5dae-80df-2b3d345ec53d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af081fd9-07d5-5dae-80df-2b3d345ec53d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469769} :answer-field/id #uuid "62d9c045-d88c-5e07-8963-4b9cc131c95f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470496}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2a943335-01cc-5c39-a96e-fdeaef543401" :question/math-academy-id "q-95251" :question/problem "Which of the following vector spaces are finite-dimensional?\n- **I.** ${\\text{M}}_{250\\times 100}(R),$ the vector space of all $250\\times 100$ matrices over $R$\n- **II.** $R[t],$ the vector space of all polynomial functions in the variable $t$\n- **III.** ${R}_{10}[t],$ the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $10$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our vector spaces.\n\n- $R[t]$ is *not* finite-dimensional. To understand why, we first note that the following set of (polynomial) functions is linearly independent:\n\n$$\n{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,…,{t}^{n}},\\,n\\in N.\n$$\n\nIndeed, we have that \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n}{a}_{i}{t}^{i}=0\n$$\n\nfor all $t\\in R$ if and only if ${a}_{i}=0$ for all $i=0,1,2,…,n.$ Therefore,  for any  $n\\in N,$  there exists a linearly independent subset of $R[t]$ of size $n,$ which imples that $R[t]$ cannot have finite dimension.\n\n- ${\\text{M}}_{250\\times 100}(R)$ and ${R}_{10}[t]$ are finite-dimensional. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{250\\times 100}(R))=250\\cdot 100=25\\,000\n$$\n\n \nand\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{10}[t])=10+1=11,\n$$\n\nare both finite numbers.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360596 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133791 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e81030a-0151-5dea-b9bc-74aae2499482" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Orthogonal Projection Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b658f65a-661f-595c-8477-1e49bceba6be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469770} {:answer/id #uuid "e0ede162-4f91-520b-9d3f-025e55bc5aaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0ede162-4f91-520b-9d3f-025e55bc5aaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469771} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed786c32-96b5-5306-9877-28d72592f72c" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470497} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6c1edc6-99ab-54aa-ab9e-f95a49fcfa76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469772} {:answer/id #uuid "99a30c17-5581-5fc8-b85a-5919565085bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6c1edc6-99ab-54aa-ab9e-f95a49fcfa76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469772} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5ea01e1-41c7-533c-bc77-ccf22a1bf6fd" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470498} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f687c01-7e57-5b27-83cd-fe8161fc79a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469774} {:answer/id #uuid "94a9724f-7830-5ca7-88a2-2feb8f9b31d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f687c01-7e57-5b27-83cd-fe8161fc79a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469774} :answer-field/id #uuid "257cf9ba-643d-5a9e-a3c0-437571a8a32b" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470499}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ea1f03fd-61df-5261-a45a-0d8c938b6ee9" :question/math-academy-id "q-95346" :question/problem "Which of the following are orthogonal projection matrices?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5} & -\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5} & -\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $Q$ is an orthogonal projection matrix if and only if ${Q}^{2}=Q$ and ${Q}^{T}=Q.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is an orthogonal projection matrix. Indeed,\n${A}^{T}=A$\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5} & -\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5} & -\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -10 \\\\ -10 & 20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5} & -\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is *not* an orthogonal projection matrix. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{T}\\ne B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is *not* an orthogonal projection matrix. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{T}\\ne C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360597 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133791 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e81030a-0151-5dea-b9bc-74aae2499482" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Orthogonal Projection Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d91dccf7-f768-50e6-8a72-b5da6c89a6dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469776} {:answer/id #uuid "d988b436-508d-5483-923d-6e920aead5b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d91dccf7-f768-50e6-8a72-b5da6c89a6dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469776} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cb60a94-72a5-5abf-a80d-5254f6849783" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470500} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc5b511c-8e27-53d7-8170-a24e73154bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469778} {:answer/id #uuid "d87b13c6-a7c9-52cc-8e0f-17793de6e654" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d87b13c6-a7c9-52cc-8e0f-17793de6e654" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469779} :answer-field/id #uuid "e20ce85b-3034-5756-bb6e-2ec399fa2ad5" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470501} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b734095-0a53-5925-9d7d-535a13104c4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469780} {:answer/id #uuid "05d4aa39-5d9e-5f04-85c9-616f65a4e8ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b734095-0a53-5925-9d7d-535a13104c4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469780} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa635a58-22e5-54c4-818a-1265728bed9d" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470502}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a3f5c5d3-e02d-5016-8de5-5fb09c5bfb03" :question/math-academy-id "q-95351" :question/problem "Which of the following are orthogonal projection matrices?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{10} & -\\frac{3}{10} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{10} & \\frac{1}{10}\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $Q$ is an orthogonal projection matrix if and only if ${Q}^{2}=Q$ and ${Q}^{T}=Q.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is *not* an orthogonal projection matrix. We have\n${A}^{T}=A$\nbut \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is an orthogonal projection matrix. Indeed,\n${B}^{T}=B$\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{2} & =B\\cdot B \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{10} & -\\frac{3}{10} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{10} & \\frac{1}{10}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{10} & -\\frac{3}{10} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{10} & \\frac{1}{10}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}9 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}9 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{100}[\\begin{aligned}9 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}9 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{100}[\\begin{aligned}90 & -30 \\\\ -30 & 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{10} & -\\frac{3}{10} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{10} & \\frac{1}{10}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is *not* an orthogonal projection matrix. We have\n${C}^{T}=C$\nbut \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{2} & =C\\cdot C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}13 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360598 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133791 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e81030a-0151-5dea-b9bc-74aae2499482" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Orthogonal Projection Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b15702d8-832c-5c42-9e03-35bd6362356e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469782} {:answer/id #uuid "a8c4e376-6efd-522b-8eb7-f7615e94db55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b15702d8-832c-5c42-9e03-35bd6362356e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469782} :answer-field/id #uuid "974cd089-5644-58e6-a817-3fcd5bd1e784" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470503} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03864ad4-b006-5fc9-8fa0-0354cf3608d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469784} {:answer/id #uuid "0104f927-d60f-53d4-8da5-b850cb12b81e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0104f927-d60f-53d4-8da5-b850cb12b81e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469785} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e4c9dc5-f54d-5159-9354-74e7c37cd4fe" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470504} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8b1894b-ee6f-56ab-bc55-9c3a60a64104" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469786} {:answer/id #uuid "0858c5b8-44e1-52d9-ad2f-bad245893839" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8b1894b-ee6f-56ab-bc55-9c3a60a64104" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469786} :answer-field/id #uuid "aef2b943-2022-5757-b8a1-588037d10a51" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470505}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ed3b258-fab2-58a0-b1d7-42245fa9a9bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-95353" :question/problem "Which of the following are orthogonal projection matrices?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{13} & \\frac{6}{13} \\\\ -\\frac{6}{13} & \\frac{4}{13}\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{26} & \\frac{5}{26} \\\\ \\frac{5}{26} & \\frac{25}{26}\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $Q$ is an orthogonal projection matrix if and only if ${Q}^{2}=Q$ and ${Q}^{T}=Q.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is *not* an orthogonal projection matrix. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\ne A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is an orthogonal projection matrix. We have\n${B}^{T}=B$\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{2} & =B\\cdot B \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{26} & \\frac{5}{26} \\\\ \\frac{5}{26} & \\frac{25}{26}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{26} & \\frac{5}{26} \\\\ \\frac{5}{26} & \\frac{25}{26}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 25\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 25\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{676}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 25\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 25\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{676}[\\begin{aligned}26 & 130 \\\\ 130 & 650\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{26} & \\frac{5}{26} \\\\ \\frac{5}{26} & \\frac{25}{26}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is *not* an orthogonal projection matrix. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{T}\\ne C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360600 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152221 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e609aabf-7e7e-5997-b8dc-c66e7a14a36f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Finite and Infinite-Dimensional Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0366f0a7-9dc5-5a50-9987-2d20cf430407" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469788} {:answer/id #uuid "85c5de64-419d-5402-86fe-df0bcd87ab34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85c5de64-419d-5402-86fe-df0bcd87ab34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469789} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f298414-5a78-5758-b95a-22a8e18aef9c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470506} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5d5d3fa-0ab9-5849-9ca3-e919738f22d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469790} {:answer/id #uuid "0ecfa01d-9146-57fe-b075-031b2950c441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ecfa01d-9146-57fe-b075-031b2950c441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469791} :answer-field/id #uuid "50410e2b-8fd6-5841-ae1c-d3b21473606c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470507} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0482d56-7be1-5926-a311-a997c9be84df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469792} {:answer/id #uuid "9fb2846f-3268-586a-ad2f-121bcef06817" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0482d56-7be1-5926-a311-a997c9be84df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469792} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c36212a-1538-522d-a072-6f8372621105" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470508}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e531c342-c218-5c9e-86de-28e412cdeaaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-95386" :question/problem "Which of the following vector spaces are finite-dimensional?\n- **I.** ${R}^{150}$\n- **II.** ${\\text{M}}_{150}(R),$ the vector space of all $150\\times 150$ matrices over $R$\n- **III.** $R[t],$ the vector space of all polynomial functions in the variable $t$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our vector spaces.\n\n- ${R}^{150}$ and ${\\text{M}}_{150}(R)$ are finite-dimensional. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{150})=150\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{150}(R))={150}^{2}=22\\,500,\n$$\n\n \nare both finite numbers.\n\n- $R[t]$ is *not* finite-dimensional. To understand why, we first note that the following set of (polynomial) functions is linearly independent:\n\n$$\n{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,…,{t}^{n}},\\,n\\in N.\n$$\n\nIndeed, we have that \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n}{a}_{i}{t}^{i}=0\n$$\n\nfor all $t\\in R$ if and only if ${a}_{i}=0$ for all $i=0,1,2,…,n.$ Therefore,  for any  $n\\in N,$  there exists a linearly independent subset of $R[t]$ of size $n,$ which imples that $R[t]$ cannot have finite dimension.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360671 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166788 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a6ca425-0e94-5b83-8729-fda13fbf3d7d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equilibrium Solutions of a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8139637-8e82-5b32-b05d-a90a5ed25604" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469806} {:answer/id #uuid "a6b99b14-815f-5b95-84f7-bf5e12833ebe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6b99b14-815f-5b95-84f7-bf5e12833ebe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469807} :answer-field/id #uuid "792054a2-6470-5383-8af1-815b20b190b7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470515} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18b5002f-0058-5055-8f76-cd09fc58fc68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469808} {:answer/id #uuid "ea5cd59b-8c99-5170-8de8-87b5f99f1eca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18b5002f-0058-5055-8f76-cd09fc58fc68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469808} :answer-field/id #uuid "86b22de7-7fe7-5dd4-b362-42d2cacff149" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470516} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c45e6e66-7fbc-5337-9c2b-a5fa36cf9618" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469810} {:answer/id #uuid "308fcee5-5e70-5885-b5ea-20cdebf40a6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469811}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c45e6e66-7fbc-5337-9c2b-a5fa36cf9618" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469810} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3426a6c-4972-5b04-aaed-80a5d1606fef" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470517}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4bdcd03c-4e33-5af2-a43a-72ec614b803e" :question/math-academy-id "q-96070" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+y={y}^{2}-2.$ Which of the following is an equilibrium solution of this equation?\n- **I.** $y=2$\n- **II.** $y=1$\n- **III.** $y=4$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given an autonomous differential equation ${y}^{′}(t)=f(y),$ if there exists a constant $c$ such that $f(c)=0,$ then $y=c$ is an equilibrium solution of the equation.\n\nFirst, we write the given equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}={y}^{2}-y-2,\n$$\n\nand we get that $f(y)={y}^{2}-y-2.$\n\nNow, let's check each proposed solution by substituting them into $f(y).$\n\n- $y=2$ is an equilibrium point. We have $f(2)={2}^{2}-2-2=0.$$\\,✓$\n\n- $y=1$ is *not* an equilibrium point. We have $f(1)={1}^{2}-1-2=-2\\ne 0.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- $y=4$ is *not* an equilibrium point. We have $f(4)={4}^{2}-4-2=10\\ne 0.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360672 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166788 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a6ca425-0e94-5b83-8729-fda13fbf3d7d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equilibrium Solutions of a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e089712-9e8d-5a06-9486-b36e393637d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469812} {:answer/id #uuid "e5af46c0-36b4-5041-b26e-4967d1519a68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e089712-9e8d-5a06-9486-b36e393637d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469812} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0be3825-bbe9-533b-835f-a228584ff886" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470518} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "260410a8-65bb-5892-aa51-d356fbb9b5a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469814} {:answer/id #uuid "2431bdce-8758-5311-bac2-20c5ea1f09ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2431bdce-8758-5311-bac2-20c5ea1f09ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469815} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7b1200c-89e7-56eb-8bd9-0a9a36df85a5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470519} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ceb5c2b-15b4-5a91-8b04-6a949d64834d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469816} {:answer/id #uuid "7f9bff13-8c86-5ea9-a24a-7a92868f1e4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ceb5c2b-15b4-5a91-8b04-6a949d64834d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469816} :answer-field/id #uuid "eca4bcc5-b73b-5b70-b7a2-6076a97d7f00" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470520}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7617131b-e756-503f-ac7c-f76ae1870fab" :question/math-academy-id "q-96072" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{2}={y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y.$ Which of the following is an equilibrium solution of this equation?\n- **I.** $y=1$\n- **II.** $y=e$\n- **III.** $y=2$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given an autonomous differential equation ${y}^{′}(x)=f(y),$ if there exists a constant $c$ such that $f(c)=0,$ then $y=c$ is an equilibrium solution of the equation.\n\nFirst, we write the given equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-{e}^{2},\n$$\n\nand we get that $f(y)={y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-{e}^{2}.$\n\nNow, let's check each proposed solution by substituting them into $f(y).$\n\n- $y=1$ is *not* an equilibrium point. We have $f(1)=(1)^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡1-{e}^{2}=-{e}^{2}\\ne 0.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- $y=e$ is an equilibrium point. We have $f(e)={e}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡e-{e}^{2}={e}^{2}-{e}^{2}=0.$$\\,✓$\n\n- $y=2$ is *not* an equilibrium point. We have $f(2)={2}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-{e}^{2}\\ne 0.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360703 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172031 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbac348b-629f-52a1-9bb3-0d3f8483ff44" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Arrow Function Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9b6f5fe-376c-566e-ba05-659e9ea6ba82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469818} {:answer/id #uuid "52ca3482-feed-59d4-b538-a9a963ff0364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9b6f5fe-376c-566e-ba05-659e9ea6ba82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469818} :answer-field/id #uuid "92ef3647-f3bc-58b6-b6f2-6136feea2c86" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470521} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "565877fc-84c4-599d-b36c-354d310b66a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469820} {:answer/id #uuid "aacf8e8f-d8f5-5c29-88a9-56b2bf2c786d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "565877fc-84c4-599d-b36c-354d310b66a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469820} :answer-field/id #uuid "fef17412-fbf6-5e88-8671-e1ebddda8721" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470522} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4ac8ea0-e6f4-5ed1-be82-04705b4507e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469822} {:answer/id #uuid "fce9c568-b4fb-5ed7-b8ed-c9ae293016c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fce9c568-b4fb-5ed7-b8ed-c9ae293016c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469823} :answer-field/id #uuid "57633b9c-2f82-52d2-81a0-8fd4e494bf0f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470523}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8834e73f-e91c-5d8c-8257-a000ef7a9e06" :question/math-academy-id "q-96741" :question/problem "Which of the following functions has the codomain ${-1,1}?$\n- **I.** $p:{-1,1}\\to R$\n- **II.** $q:R\\to [-1,1)$\n- **III.** $r:[-1,1)\\to {-1,1}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The codomain of $p$ is $R,$ the set of real numbers.\n\n- The codomain of $q$ is $[-1,1),$ the interval from $-1$ to $1$ (including $-1$ but not including $1$).\n\n- The codomain of $r$ is ${-1,1},$ the set containing the two numbers $-1$ and $1$ only.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360704 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172031 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbac348b-629f-52a1-9bb3-0d3f8483ff44" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Arrow Function Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ae73709-fe5b-5f16-9b74-31dec32ca855" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469824} {:answer/id #uuid "1eb7d921-a5c2-5849-8662-36a792a6e641" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1eb7d921-a5c2-5849-8662-36a792a6e641" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469825} :answer-field/id #uuid "beef1889-063a-50cc-b883-c9539c59ae0f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470524} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e3b76c4-13e1-56b2-91e8-5ebcaa86f30a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469826} {:answer/id #uuid "1c1e6d97-ec46-5e8b-a3c8-af719a4324a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e3b76c4-13e1-56b2-91e8-5ebcaa86f30a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469826} :answer-field/id #uuid "1dd0189d-5a3c-5376-ab84-cc0225b43b23" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470525} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb18571f-ffb9-534f-b17f-c1edf1fc4a16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469828} {:answer/id #uuid "e6c81153-33a5-54db-8708-0c0a04623fe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6c81153-33a5-54db-8708-0c0a04623fe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469829} :answer-field/id #uuid "41232518-2643-5c33-bc8a-52c436568496" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e229a9e2-9edb-5a3d-981b-1fe2de7365a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-96744" :question/problem "Which of the following functions has the codomain $(-2,2]?$\n- **I.** $p:(-2,2]\\to (-2,2]$\n- **II.** $q:R\\to [-2,2)$\n- **III.** $r:[-2,2)\\to (-2,2]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The codomain of $p$ is $(-2,2],$ the interval from $-2$ to $2$ (including $2$ but not including $-2$).\n\n- The codomain of $q$ is $[-2,2),$ the interval from $-2$ to $2$ (including $-2$ but not including $2$).\n\n- The codomain of $r$ is $(-2,2],$ the interval from $-2$ to $2$ (including $2$ but not including $-2$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360705 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172031 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbac348b-629f-52a1-9bb3-0d3f