nswer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470553}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae6d946d-9a9f-5816-82c2-7048c4392f45" :question/math-academy-id "q-96857" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,-1),(-2,1),$ and $(3,0).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$ \n- **I.** $(1,3)$\n- **II.** $(0,-3)$\n- **III.** $(2,3)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 3 & 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-3,-9),$  $(1,3)$, and $(3,9).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \" I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360779 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172036 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1343e4de-56ee-563c-bdc8-f8c0cdc54f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Slope Fields"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0006d664-b8ff-5634-986f-5c0d4e1d7dad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469884} {:answer/id #uuid "83c6dacd-fb1e-5471-803a-abd44bac5e0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.